rom each other in  general but you're right  things are much more normal in sweden  they took a different strategy  uh they are in a different place um but  it was  at high expense at the beginning in an  interview you said  how much virus you breathe in is  probably one of the most important  determinants of  how sick you get do you still stand by  that  yes you know we and others have been  looking at that question  of the viral dose or the viral inoculum  the amount that you get in  is proportional to how sick you get and  we've not only been looking at this with  chronovirus this is actually  been shown in measles dengue salmonella  many other infectious diseases  we're putting together a review paper on  this now but the main thing is that if  this is true with coronavirus  social distancing and wearing that mask  reduces the amount of virus you get in  and the likelihood that you're going to  become ill and this  seems to make sense in animal models  um and what we've been seeing with this  virus including decreasing mortality  in places that are consistent with  facial masking  monica two quick questions for you what  do you think about your  president's message that he's sending to  the rest of the world  i think uh president trump's message is  dangerous  and ridiculous and he has been um  flouted almost all public health  recommendations except for testing he  doesn't mask he doesn't socially  distance  he keeps large crowds he doesn't contact  trace in the case of this disaster he  didn't isolate  he didn't encourage quarantining he just  tested  that is only one strategy of the  pandemic and it's not enough  and and lastly if you can sum it up in  in one word  what's going to end this pandemic  you know it is not being normal for  at least a year plus the vaccine on top  of it so it is  wearing masks staying away from each  other hand washing  um and then waiting for that safe and  effective vaccine  but not completely shutting down society  you heard it from monica gandhi thank  you very much for being on the show  today  thank you and now it's derek williams  chance to answer your questions on the  coronavirus  if you want us to look into something in  particular just write to us on our  youtube channel  if i've recovered from covid19 do i  still have to wear a mask  sometimes it's easy to forget that that  millions and millions of people  worldwide have also  recovered from covet 19 and want to  return as much as possible  to life as usual but what does coming  out the other end  mean um are you safe from the disease  because you're immune  can you still pose a potential danger to  others do you need to continue to social  distance and  and and wear a mask it's all questions  that we still don't have  a firm answers to we just have to guess  and rely on  what we know from other infectious  diseases particularly  those caused by other coronaviruses  based on what we've seen so far with  covet 19 people do acquire  some immunity the problem is we don't  know for how long  on average what we do know is that with  other coronaviruses that infect humans  immunity can wane pretty swiftly  there are a number of studies that  convincingly show  that people can be reinfected with some  of them within a year  and there have been a few isolated  documented cases  of that also happening with covid19 also  at least in some of those cases the  people who were reinfected  showed no symptoms the second time  around so  were they infectious to others we don't  know  and to me it seems like in general that  until we have  better data when it comes to questions  that we have to answer with  we don't know we should be airing on the  side of caution  so in the face of this particular  we don't know i'd go for the fallback  position which is to continue to assume  that masking up is a way to protect  yourself  and others even if you've recovered from  covid19  [Music]
 

